  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1228 PM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nBlue skies and a visible sun are a welcomed change. The upper \npattern flow shows trofing over the Big Bend Country of west \nTexas and weak ridging over the Rockies as revealed by WV \nimagery. At the sfc, high pressure has settled into the Upper \nMidwest and has spilled into Nebraska and Kansas. Wind speeds \nare generally out of the northeast at about 5-10 knots. \n\nTemperatures this afternoon have outpaced the forecast diurnal\ntrend, so afternoon max temps have been pushed up by two\ndegrees. It matters to few beyond the weather weenies. It's a\nbeautiful day either way. \n\nSkies remain clear tonight and through the weekend with little\nto no impactful weather forecast. With the wet soil and sfc high\nin the area, entertained the thought of fog development\novernight, but the considerably drier air in place means dewpoint\ndepressions should remain above zero. Fog will also be battling\nthe wind speeds beginning to creep up after midnight, \nespecially north.",
